// expect-result: [7,7,7]
// Decided detail 225 (loop round 1, ASTRA-3): a producer's Stream requirements
// are its body's without Scope, because the Stream's callback supplies that
// Scope, as Stream.callback does. Forking a scoped child inside a producer
// asks the consumer for no Scope; another service stays. The declaration
// output is pinned in expected/main.d.ts, and each consumption of the Stream
// runs the body again.
import { poll, needsDb } from "./held.ts"
export interface Db { readonly name: string }
export effect function* scopedItem() {
  const child = try Effect.forkScoped(poll)
  yield 7
}
export effect function* withDb() {
  const n = try needsDb
  const child = try Effect.forkScoped(poll)
  yield n
}
export effect function* plainItem() {
  yield 7
}
export effect function main() {
  const first = try Stream.runFold(scopedItem(), () => 0, (sum: number, x: number) => sum + x)
  const second = try Stream.runFold(scopedItem(), () => 0, (sum: number, x: number) => sum + x)
  const plain = try Stream.runFold(plainItem(), () => 0, (sum: number, x: number) => sum + x)
  return [first, second, plain]
}

// docs/design/vips/0021-producers.md#c23128e912ee385f | VIP-21 inferred-requirements-exclude-provided-Scope
// **Amended 2026-10-30: inferred producer requirements.** Infer the body requirements `RBody` as for an `Effect`, then expose `Exclude<RBody, Scope.Scope>` on the `Stream`: the accepted `Stream.callback` supplies its `Scope`.

// docs/design/vips/0021-producers.md#756fdaf1d9beacf8 | VIP-21 inferred-requirements-exclude-provided-Scope
// **A producer's inferred requirements exclude the Scope supplied by its accepted Stream callback.** (Opus round28 m44; accepted VIP-21/VIP-32 counterpart.) Infer the producer body with the existing Effect/producer rules, then expose environment `Exclude<R, Scope.Scope>` on the resulting `Stream.Stream<A, E, ...>`, exactly as pinned Effect4.1.0 `Stream.callback` does.

// docs/design/vips/0021-producers.md#50072a1c838132a5 | VIP-21 inferred-requirements-exclude-provided-Scope
// Its callback already receives `R | Scope.Scope`; a producer's `fork.scoped` therefore does not impose an external Scope requirement just because the same operation in an ordinary unscoped Effect body would.

// docs/design/vips/0021-producers.md#395fdebfb1368b71 | VIP-21 inferred-requirements-exclude-provided-Scope
// ```vibe effect function* values() { fork.scoped never // Scope is supplied by the accepted producer counterpart yield 1 } // inferred Stream.Stream<number>; callers need no external Scope for this body ``` Effect TS: ```ts const values = Stream.callback<number>(queue => Effect.gen(function* () { yield* Effect.forkScoped(Effect.never) yield* Queue.offer(queue, 1) yield* Queue.end(queue) }), { bufferSize: 1, strategy: "suspend" }) // Stream<number, never, never> ``` Decided by the agent from accepted VIP-21's exact `Stream.callback` counterpart, VIP-32's Effect4.1.0 pin, principle1 (idiomatic Effect provides this Scope) and principle2 (the pinned generic signature determines the environment), 2026-10-30.
